{
	title: 'Sessions message each other; the user comes first',
	description: "The user's idea (questions.md item 7), to be designed with him before building. Every message says who sent it: the user, or another session (by id and name); the model and every client can always tell another session from the user, and the user takes priority. Two kinds: (1) advisory: another session's message does not steer; if the recipient is working it arrives attached to its next tool result, if idle the recipient sees it as a message from that session; (2) steering: a session may steer others like the user can, for the user's needs or an emergency ('stop all action in tabs 10-15 immediately'). The sender is set by the host, never trusted from the client. Up never recalls messages from other sessions (task for Up edits).",
